# 14. Test microservice communication

This is the **most important exercise**.

Get an order Pod:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

Copy its name.

Then:

```bash
kubectl exec -it ORDER_POD_NAME -- sh
```

Inside the container:

```bash
wget -qO- http://user-service:3000/users/1
```

You should get:

```json
{
  "id": "1",
  "name": "Nabajyoti",
  "email": "nabajyoti@example.com"
}
```

Then:

```bash
wget -qO- http://product-service:3000/products/101
```

You should get:

```json
{
  "id": "101",
  "name": "Laptop",
  "price": 85000
}
```

That demonstrates:

```text
Order Pod
   │
   │ DNS
   ▼
user-service
   │
   ▼
User Pod
```

and:

```text
Order Pod
   │
   │ DNS
   ▼
product-service
   │
   ▼
Product Pod
```

