## 19. One important improvement

For your learning exercise, **HTTP REST communication** is perfect.

For a production architecture, however, I'd eventually introduce:

```text
                    Microservices
                         │
              ┌──────────┴──────────┐
              │                     │
          Synchronous          Asynchronous
              │                     │
           REST/gRPC          Pub/Sub/Kafka
              │                     │
        Request/Response          Events
```

For example:

```text
POST /orders
     │
     ▼
order-service
     │
     ├── REST → user-service
     │
     └── REST → product-service
     │
     ▼
OrderCreated event
     │
     ▼
     Pub/Sub
     │
     ├── notification-service
     ├── inventory-service
     └── analytics-service
```

That will take you from a basic Kubernetes exercise to a **real enterprise microservices architecture**.

If you follow this sequence—**Docker → Artifact Registry → GKE → ClusterIP → DNS → Pod-to-Pod communication → Ingress → Helm → HPA → Pub/Sub/Kafka**—you'll cover the core GCP Kubernetes deployment skills you're looking to build.
